# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and edit. Everything here is optional — with no
# `.env` at all, every script, hook, and build in this repo runs on defaults
# that are local and self-contained, and none of them point at anyone else's
# hosting account.
#
# Two loaders read this file automatically, so there is no flag to pass and no
# `export FOO=... ./script.sh` to remember:
#
#   scripts/env.sh              shell scripts and git hooks
#   website/scripts/load-env.js anything in website/ that runs on Node
#
# Both read this file first, then `website/.env`, so site-specific values
# override shared ones. Both leave an already-exported variable alone, so a CI
# secret or a one-off `FOO=bar npm run ...` always wins over the file.
#
# Site configuration (SITE_URL, ELEVENLABS_*) belongs in `website/.env` —
# see website/.env.example. It is read from here too, but keeping it next to
# the site it configures is the convention.

# --- Xcode / app signing -----------------------------------------------------
# The app's real signing seam is the git-ignored
# app/Config/Signing.local.xcconfig (see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md), which is what
# both Xcode and xcodebuild read. Setting the same names here as environment
# variables also works — xcodebuild takes build settings from the environment,
# and scripts/open-xcode.sh loads this file before launching Xcode so the GUI
# build sees them too. Prefer the xcconfig; use these only for a one-off build.
#
#   DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=ABCDE12345
#   BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX=com.yourname

# --- Crash reporting (optional, and off unless the *user* opts in too) --------
# Same shape as signing above: the real seam is the git-ignored
# app/Config/Sentry.local.xcconfig, which app/Config/Sentry.xcconfig includes.
# Setting SENTRY_DSN as an environment variable works for a one-off xcodebuild.
#
# A DSN is not a credential — it is a write-only ingest endpoint that ships in
# the app bundle by necessity — but it names one deployment's Sentry project,
# so it stays out of tracked files. Configuring it does NOT start sending
# anything: reporting also needs Settings → Diagnostics → "Send crash reports",
# which is off by default and is the actual consent gate. See docs/PRIVACY.md
# and TODO.md → "Sentry — environment variables and how to get each one".
#
# The /$()/ is required, not a typo: Xcode's xcconfig parser treats // as a
# comment anywhere on a line, including inside a URL. It is unnecessary here in
# a .env file, but keeping one form avoids copying the broken one into the
# xcconfig by mistake.
#
#   SENTRY_DSN=https:/$()/<key>@<org-id>.ingest.us.sentry.io/<project-id>

# --- Git hook tuning ---------------------------------------------------------
# The post-commit / post-checkout hooks refresh the CodeGraph index with an
# incremental `codegraph sync`, backgrounded and advisory — a hook never fails
# a commit that is already written. It takes no environment knobs, so there is
# nothing to set here; this section is kept as the documented home for hook
# tuning if a future hook needs one.
#
# The GRAPHIFY_* variables that used to live here were removed on 2026-08-18
# when Graphify was retired. Nothing reads them any more — delete them from
# your local .env if you still have them.
